# Run on a VPS

Both VPS paths are deployments. They set `L30_DEPLOYED=1`, require `L30_INITIAL_PASSWORD`, reject `last30` and disable password reset.

Keep the app on `127.0.0.1` and put a TLS proxy in front. Never expose port 4477 directly to the internet.

## Docker

CI builds the image and publishes it to GitHub Container Registry:

<CopyCommand command="docker pull ghcr.io/emmraan/last30days-news:latest" />

Run it with a named volume for `/data` and an initial password:

<CopyCommand
	command="docker run -d --name last30days-news -p 127.0.0.1:4477:4477 -v last30days-data:/data -e L30_INITIAL_PASSWORD='choose-a-password' ghcr.io/emmraan/last30days-news:latest"
/>

The image sets `L30_DEPLOYED=1`, runs as UID 1000 and stores data in `/data`. If the package is not public yet, log in first with a GitHub token that can read packages:

<CopyCommand command="echo $GITHUB_TOKEN | docker login ghcr.io -u YOUR_GITHUB_USER --password-stdin" />

For a quick check from your own machine, use an SSH tunnel:

<CopyCommand command="ssh -L 4477:127.0.0.1:4477 user@your-host" />

Then open `http://127.0.0.1:4477`. If you bind-mount a host directory instead of a named volume, make it writable by UID 1000. The container warns if `/data` is not a mounted volume, because data would disappear with the container.

To update, pull the new image and recreate the container. The volume keeps the database.

## systemd

1. Install Node.js 26.13.0 and pnpm 12.16.1 on the host.
2. Create the service user and directories:

<CopyCommand
	command="sudo useradd --system --home /var/lib/last30days-news --shell /usr/sbin/nologin last30days && sudo mkdir -p /opt/last30days-news /var/lib/last30days-news && sudo chown -R last30days:last30days /opt/last30days-news /var/lib/last30days-news"
/>

3. Clone and build as the service user:

<CopyCommand
	command="sudo -u last30days git clone https://github.com/Emmraan/last30days-news.git /opt/last30days-news && cd /opt/last30days-news && sudo -u last30days pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && sudo -u last30days pnpm build"
/>

4. Create the environment file and add `L30_INITIAL_PASSWORD`:

<CopyCommand
	command="sudo install -m 600 -o root -g root /dev/null /etc/last30days-news.env && sudoedit /etc/last30days-news.env"
/>

```text
L30_INITIAL_PASSWORD=choose-a-password
```

5. Install and start the unit:

<CopyCommand
	command="sudo cp deploy/last30days-news.service /etc/systemd/system/ && sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl enable --now last30days-news && sudo systemctl status last30days-news"
/>

6. Put a TLS proxy in front of `127.0.0.1:4477`. A minimal Caddyfile:

```text
news.example.com {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4477
}
```

The unit already sets `L30_DEPLOYED=1`, `HOST=127.0.0.1` and `L30_TRUST_PROXY=1`. Only keep `L30_TRUST_PROXY=1` when the proxy overwrites `X-Forwarded-For` and `X-Forwarded-Proto`. If it does not, remove that line so clients cannot spoof their address.

## Update

For systemd, pull the new code, rebuild and restart:

<CopyCommand
	command="cd /opt/last30days-news && sudo -u last30days git pull && sudo -u last30days pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && sudo -u last30days pnpm build && sudo systemctl restart last30days-news"
/>

The database stays in `/var/lib/last30days-news`.

